# Global saved emotions

When a user adds a **custom emotion** (via "Other — type your own") anywhere in Ledger, it must be remembered **globally** for every form that reports emotions.

## Storage

- Use a single `localStorage` key: `ledger_saved_emotions`
- All emotion pickers must read from and write to this key (via `emotion_wheel_picker` macro)

## Behavior

- Custom emotions are saved automatically when used — no opt-in checkbox
- Built-in wheel emotions are never duplicated into saved storage
- Saved emotions appear in the **Saved** category on every picker (check-in, diary card extras, thought record, etc.)
- Removing a saved emotion from one picker removes it globally
- Pickers listen for `ledger-saved-emotions-changed` and `storage` events to stay in sync on the same page or across tabs

## When adding emotion UI

- Reuse `templates/macros/emotion_wheel.html` — do not create separate saved-emotion storage
- Do not introduce alternate keys or server-side-only custom emotion lists for picker UI
